{"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"8da8dbcb70e700d9e35970e8b662b1be2c29afdc","body":"Healthy outbox channels previously waited behind a slow channel, including a measured ~200-second Forum binding phase. The reconciler now runs up to three independently supervised channel loops over the existing ordered pass, preserving claim locks, per-instance order, stable idempotency keys, HTTP timeouts, retry and dead-letter behavior.\n\nValidation and attribution:\n\n- Preserved same-fixture RED: healthy kick/wake settled at 200063/200086 ms; initial GREEN both 23 ms. Fresh sustained slow Forum/Kick/Wake tests keep healthy progress at 23–24 ms initially and 22–42 ms later.\n- Fresh outbox 22/22 rc0; library 269 passed / 1 existing ignored / rc0. Reused R4 prerequisite suite 28/28 rc0 and passed binary evidence after 468/468 input hashes matched.\n- Full R4 cargo remains 1324 passed / 10 failed / 1 ignored, rc101. Exact clean 8aa864a control reproduces all ten group67 failures by name, source coordinate and error: 9 Unavailable and 1 HTTP 422 admission_legacy_input. The R5 user mandate explicitly excludes this attributed pre-existing set from this delivery gate. No tests were removed, skipped or weakened for 67. Clean 8aa already includes the earlier product patch; this control establishes pre-existence relative to the uncommitted R3/R4 increment, not an original-main runtime comparison.\n- Candidate preserved/restored using exact task stash; 814/814 file hashes match. Original raw failures retained. Both newly owned loopback PG16 clusters stopped with actual rc0.\n- Independent affected-contract review by /root/r5_review: bounded gate PASS, blockers 0, proven Spec gaps 0; exact committed-head review and publication coordinates will be added below.\n\nReceipt: [RECEIPT-1359-OUTBOX.md](https://github.com/mayf3/svc-workflow/blob/fix/outbox-channel-isolation/RECEIPT-1359-OUTBOX.md). Attribution/raw results: [R5 evidence](https://github.com/mayf3/svc-workflow/blob/fix/outbox-channel-isolation/docs/evidence/1359-r5/ATTRIBUTION.md). Historical full-suite failure remains [R4 raw](https://github.com/mayf3/svc-workflow/blob/fix/outbox-channel-isolation/docs/evidence/1359-r4/full.log).\n\nBase main; no merge or production activation is authorized or performed. No rebase, governance edit, deployment/config/backlog operation or unrelated admission repair.\n","headRefName":"fix/outbox-channel-isolation","headRefOid":"596aaa56a811f70b6c921006ca7c83885ff710cd","isDraft":false,"mergeable":"MERGEABLE","mergedAt":null,"number":132,"state":"OPEN","title":"fix(outbox): isolate polling across delivery channels","url":"https://github.com/mayf3/svc-workflow/pull/132"}
